                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1765912593774"
                  },
                  "code": "GETDEMANDEXCEPTIONS",
                  "id": "1765912510857",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1768219874108_1",
                      "name": "planId",
                      "type": "number",
                      "value": "{{$context.$variables.PlanId}}"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1768219874109_2",
                      "name": "demandOrderNumbers",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "{{ \"[\" + $context.$nodes.WORKFLOWITERATION.$currentItem.rows.find(row => row.TableName === \"MSC_DEMANDS\" && row.OrderNumberList.length > 0).OrderNumberList + \"]\" }}"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1768219874110_3",
                      "name": "supplyOrderNumbers",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "[]"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "1768219874111_4",
                      "name": "exceptionArr",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "{{$context.$variables.demandExceptionArr}}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{}",
                  "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                        "reasoning_effort": "low"
                      },
                      "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
                      "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
                      "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
                      "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
                    },
                    "name": "FilterDemandOrders"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1765913564311"
                  },
                  "code": "FILTERDEMANDORDERS",
                  "id": "1765912593774",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1765912593780_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are given three inputs:  \n\n1. Exception Qualification Rules — a list of exception types with their qualification criteria. {{$context.$variables.extractedRulesJson.demandOrders}}\n2. Demand Exceptions Details — a list of exceptions raised against supply orders.  {{$context.$nodes.GETDEMANDEXCEPTIONS.$output}} \n3. Order List - List of orders which are need to be classified as either Review or Release based on below classification rules. {{$context.$nodes.WORKFLOWITERATION.$currentItem.rows.find(row => row.TableName === \"MSC_DEMANDS\" && row.OrderNumberList.length > 0).OrderNumberList}}\nTask:  \nClassify every order number found in the Demand Exceptions Details into one of two categories and include exceptionId for that order in the response:  \n\n- Review → At least one exception for the order matches a rule in the Exception Qualification Rules AND satisfies the rule's qualification criteria.  \n- Release → One of the following is true:  \n  a) Exceptions exist but none match any rule in the Exception Qualification Rules, OR  \n  b) Exceptions match rules but not satisfying the criteria\n  c) If we dont find any exceptions for a given order in exception details records , we mark it as Release. \n\nProcessing Logic:  \n1. Extract all unique orderNumber , exceptionId values from the Demand Exceptions Details.  \n2. For each order:  \n   - Collect all exceptions belonging to that order.  \n   - For each exception:  \n     - Check if the exception name matches a rule in the Exception Qualification Rules.  \n     - If it matches, evaluate against the qualification criteria.  \n       Example: If the rule says \"Exception Days > 5\", then the field `minDaysLate` in the exception details must be strictly greater than 5.  \n     - If any matching exception satisfies the rule criteria → mark order as Review.  \n   - If no rules matched or none satisfied → mark order as Release.  \n3. Ensure every order from the input appears exactly once, in either Review or Release. \n4. For each order which are classified as Review , we need the order to be added in ReviewException which hold pair of order number and exceptionId(exception type numeric value) from exception record. \n5.Ensure every output has ReviewException as array of pairs {orderNumber,exceptionId}\nReview and Release output has only comma separated orderNumbers\n\n\n> Note: If an order has multiple qualifying exceptions, include **one Review entry per qualifying exception** (same orderNumber can appear multiple times in Review with different exceptionId). Do **not** include that orderNumber in Release.\n\n\n---\n\n## IMPORTANT CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS\n\n- **Never generate** an order number (even if you see a numeric sequence).  \n- Always cross-verify that the output contains **only** order numbers present in the **Supply Order List**.\n- **No order** should be present in output that is not present in the input Supply Order List.\n- Do not include the same orderNumber in both Review and Release.\n\n---\n\n\nOutput Format:  \nReturn a JSON object in exactly this format:  \n\n{\n  \"Review\": \"comma_separated_order_numbers_here\",\n  \"Release\": \"comma_separated_order_numbers_here\"\n  \"ReviewException\": \"array of pairs {orderNumber,exceptionId}\"\n}\n\n- Each key is array of order numbers except for ReviewException, key is array of Pair of {orderNumber,exceptionId}. \n- Three keys must always be present, even if empty.\n- ExceptionId is not unique for each order , it is just exception type numeric value , like 14, 23 etc , so multiple review orders with same exception id."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"OrderSet\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"Review\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"uniqueItems\": true\n    },\n    \"Release\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"uniqueItems\": true\n    },\n    \"ReviewException\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"orderNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"exceptionId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"orderNumber\", \"exceptionId\"]\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"Review\", \"Release\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
