                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                        "reasoning_effort": "low"
                      },
                      "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
                      "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
                      "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
                      "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
                    },
                    "name": "FilterSupplyOrders"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1765913837616"
                  },
                  "code": "FILTERSUPPLYORDERS",
                  "id": "1765913781611",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1765913781619_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are given 4 inputs:\n\n1. **Exception Qualification Rules** — a list of exception types with their qualification criteria.  \n   `{{$context.$variables.extractedRulesJson.supplyOrders}}`\n\n2. **Demand Exceptions Details** — a list of exceptions raised against Supply orders.  \n   `{{$context.$nodes.GETDEMANDEXCP.$output}}`\n\n3. **Supply Exceptions Details** — a list of exceptions raised against Supply orders.  \n   `{{$context.$nodes.GETSUPPLIESEXCEPTION.$output}}`\n\n4. **Supply Order List** — list of orders which need to be classified as either Review or Release based on the classification rules.  \n   `{{$context.$nodes.WORKFLOWITERATION.$currentItem.rows.find(row => row.TableName === \"MSC_SUPPLIES\" && row.OrderNumberList.length > 0).OrderNumberList}}`\n\n---\n\nTask:  \nClassify every order number found in the Exceptions Details into one of two categories and include exceptionId for that order in the response:  \n\n- Review → At least one exception for the order matches a rule in the Exception Qualification Rules AND satisfies the rule's qualification criteria.  \n- Release → One of the following is true:  \n  a) Exceptions exist but none match any rule in the Exception Qualification Rules, OR  \n  b) Exceptions match rules but not satisfying the criteria\n  c) If we dont find any exceptions for a given order in exception details records , we mark it as Release. \n\nProcessing Logic:  \n1. Extract all unique orderNumber , exceptionId values from the Demand & Supply Exceptions Details.  \n2. For each order:  \n   - Collect all exceptions belonging to that order.  \n   - For each exception:  \n     - Check if the exception name matches a rule in the Exception Qualification Rules.  \n     - If it matches, evaluate against the qualification criteria.  \n       Example: If the rule says \"Exception Days > 5\", then the field `minDaysLate` in the exception details must be strictly greater than 5.  \n     - If any matching exception satisfies the rule criteria → mark order as Review.  \n   - If no rules matched or none satisfied → mark order as Release.  \n3. Ensure every order from the input appears exactly once, in either Review or Release. \n4. For each order which are classified as Review , we need the order to be added in ReviewException which hold pair of order number and exceptionId(exception type numeric value) from exception record. \n5.Ensure every output has ReviewException as array of pairs {orderNumber,exceptionId}\nReview and Release output has only comma separated orderNumbers\n\n\n> Note: If an order has multiple qualifying exceptions, include **one Review entry per qualifying exception** (same orderNumber can appear multiple times in Review with different exceptionId). Do **not** include that orderNumber in Release.\n\n\n---\n\n## IMPORTANT CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS\n\n- **Never generate** an order number (even if you see a numeric sequence).  \n- Always cross-verify that the output contains **only** order numbers present in the **Supply Order List**.\n- **No order** should be present in output that is not present in the input Supply Order List.\n- Do not include the same orderNumber in both Review and Release.\n\n---\n\n\nOutput Format:  \nReturn a JSON object in exactly this format:  \n\n{\n  \"Review\": \"comma_separated_order_numbers_here\",\n  \"Release\": \"comma_separated_order_numbers_here\"\n  \"ReviewException\": \"array of pairs {orderNumber,exceptionId}\"\n}\n\n- Each key is array of order numbers except for ReviewException, key is array of Pair of {orderNumber,exceptionId}. \n- Three keys must always be present, even if empty.\n- ExceptionId is not unique for each order , it is just exception type numeric value , like 14, 23 etc , so multiple review orders with same exception id."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"OrderSet\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"Review\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"uniqueItems\": true\n    },\n    \"Release\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n      \"uniqueItems\": true\n    },\n    \"ReviewException\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"orderNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"exceptionId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"orderNumber\", \"exceptionId\"]\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"Review\", \"Release\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "mergeJsonCodeNode",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "const DemandOrderFilteredResults = $context.$nodes.WORKFLOWITERATION.FILTERDEMANDORDERS.$output || {Review: [], Release: [],ReviewException: []}; \nconst SupplyOrderFilteredResults = $context.$nodes.WORKFLOWITERATION.FILTERSUPPLYORDERS.$output || {Review: [], Release: [],ReviewException: []};\nconst InputJsonArray = $context.$nodes.WORKFLOWITERATION.$currentItem;\n\n// Parse InputJsonArray to extract order-to-transaction mapping\nconst inputData = InputJsonArray.rows[0];\nconst orderList = inputData.OrderNumberList.split(',').map(o => o.replace(/'/g, '').trim());\nconst transactionList = inputData.TransactionIdList.split(',').map(t => t.trim());\n\n// Create order-to-transaction mapping\nconst orderToTransaction = {};\nfor (let i = 0; i < orderList.length; i++) {\n  if (orderList[i] && transactionList[i]) {\n    orderToTransaction[orderList[i]] = String(transactionList[i]).trim();\n  }\n}\n\n// Build ReviewTransactions set - normalize all IDs to TRANSACTION IDS\nconst reviewTransactions = new Set();\n\n// DemandOrderFilteredResults.Review already assumed txIds\nif (DemandOrderFilteredResults?.Review) {\n  DemandOrderFilteredResults.Review.forEach(orderNum => {\n    const txId = orderToTransaction[orderNum];\n    if (txId != null) reviewTransactions.add(String(txId).trim());\n  });\n}\n\n// SupplyOrderFilteredResults.Review are ORDER NUMBERS → convert to txIds\nif (SupplyOrderFilteredResults?.Review) {\n  SupplyOrderFilteredResults.Review.forEach(orderNum => {\n    const txId = orderToTransaction[orderNum];\n    if (txId) {\n      reviewTransactions.add(String(txId).trim());\n    }\n  });\n}\n\n\n// Create sets for quick lookup - normalize all IDs to strings\nconst demandTransactions = new Set();\nconst supplyTransactions = new Set();\n\nif (DemandOrderFilteredResults) {\n  if (DemandOrderFilteredResults.Review) {\n    DemandOrderFilteredResults.Review.forEach(orderNum => {\n      const txId = orderToTransaction[orderNum];\n      if (txId !== null && txId !== undefined) {\n        demandTransactions.add(String(txId).trim());\n      }\n    });\n  }\n  if (DemandOrderFilteredResults.Release) {\n    DemandOrderFilteredResults.Release.forEach(orderNum => {\n      const txId = orderToTransaction[orderNum];\n      if (txId !== null && txId !== undefined) {\n        demandTransactions.add(String(txId).trim());\n      }\n    });\n  }\n}\n\nif (SupplyOrderFilteredResults) {\n  if (SupplyOrderFilteredResults.Review) {\n    SupplyOrderFilteredResults.Review.forEach(orderNum => {\n      const txId = orderToTransaction[orderNum];\n      if (txId !== null && txId !== undefined) {\n        supplyTransactions.add(String(txId).trim());\n      }\n    });\n  }\n  if (SupplyOrderFilteredResults.Release) {\n    SupplyOrderFilteredResults.Release.forEach(orderNum => {\n      const txId = orderToTransaction[orderNum];\n      if (txId !== null && txId !== undefined) {\n        supplyTransactions.add(String(txId).trim());\n      }\n    });\n  }\n}\n\n// Initialize result structure\nconst result = {\n  ByOrderNumber: {\n    DemandOrder: { Review: [], Release: [] },\n    SupplyOrder: { Review: [], Release: [] }\n  },\n  ByTransactionId: {\n    DemandOrder: { Review: [], Release: [],ReviewException: [] },\n    SupplyOrder: { Review: [], Release: [],ReviewException: [] }\n  },\n  Count: 0\n};\n\n// ---- NEW: index ReviewException by orderNumber per orderType (preserves exceptionId order within each orderNumber)\nfunction indexExceptionsByOrderNumber(reviewExceptionArr) {\n  const map = Object.create(null);\n  (reviewExceptionArr || []).forEach(ex => {\n    const orderNumber = ex?.orderNumber != null ? String(ex.orderNumber).trim() : \"\";\n    const exceptionId = ex?.exceptionId != null ? String(ex.exceptionId).trim() : \"\";\n    if (!orderNumber || !exceptionId) return;\n\n    if (!map[orderNumber]) map[orderNumber]=[];\n\n    if(map[orderNumber].length===0){\n    map[orderNumber].push(exceptionId);}\n  });\n  return map;\n}\n\nconst demandExByOrder = indexExceptionsByOrderNumber(DemandOrderFilteredResults.ReviewException);\nconst supplyExByOrder = indexExceptionsByOrderNumber(SupplyOrderFilteredResults.ReviewException);\n\n// Process each order in the exact order they appear in InputJsonArray\nfor (const orderNum of orderList) {\n  const txId = orderToTransaction[orderNum];\n  \n  // Skip malformed entries\n  if (!txId) continue;\n  \n  // Determine if Review or Release\n  const isReview = reviewTransactions.has(txId);\n  const category = isReview ? 'Review' : 'Release';\n  \n  // Determine if Demand or Supply\n  // If appears in both, prefer Supply\n  let orderType;\n  if (supplyTransactions.has(txId)) {\n    orderType = 'SupplyOrder';\n  } else if (demandTransactions.has(txId)) {\n    orderType = 'DemandOrder';\n  } else {\n    if(inputData.rows[0].TableName === 'MSC_DEMANDS'){\n      orderType = 'DemandOrder';\n    }\n    else{\n      orderType = 'SupplyOrder';\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Add to ByOrderNumber\n  result.ByOrderNumber[orderType][category].push(orderNum);\n  \n  // Add to ByTransactionId (preserve original type from mapping)\n  result.ByTransactionId[orderType][category].push(txId);\n\n   // ---- NEW: attach converted ReviewException INSIDE the Review path, in the same order as orderList\n  if (category === \"Review\") {\n    const exIds =\n      (orderType === \"DemandOrder\" ? demandExByOrder[orderNum] : supplyExByOrder[orderNum]) || [];\nconst exceptionId = exIds.length ? exIds[0] : null; \n\n     result.ByTransactionId[orderType].ReviewException.push({\n        orderNumber: String(txId).trim(),\n        exceptionId\n      });\n    \n  }\n  // Increment count if Release\n  if (!isReview) {\n    result.Count++;\n  }\n}\n\nreturn result;"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1765915872263"
                  },
                  "code": "MERGEJSONCODENODE",
                  "id": "1765913837616",
                  "inputs": [],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
                  "type": "CODE"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "isvalidToRelease"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "true": "1768852435556",
                    "false": "1770716577937"
                  },
                  "code": "ISVALIDTORELEASE",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "end_1765912054931",
                  "id": "1765915872263",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1765915872265_1",
                      "name": "condition",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "true"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "CONDITION"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Generate Payload for new rest",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "// ===== INPUTS FROM WORKFLOW =====\nvar rows = $context.$nodes.WORKFLOWITERATION.$currentItem.rows;\nvar classification = $context.$nodes.WORKFLOWITERATION.MERGEJSONCODENODE.$output.result ;   \nvar planId = $context.$variables.PlanId ;\nvar workflowRunId = $context.$variables.workflowRunId ;\n\n\n// ===== STEP 1: Parse original transaction lists =====\nvar originalSupply = [];\nvar originalDemand = [];\n\nfor (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n\n  var r = rows[i];\n\n  var txIds = [];\n  if (r.TransactionIdList) {\n    txIds = r.TransactionIdList\n      .split(\",\")\n      .map(function(s) {\n        return s.replace(/'/g, \"\").trim();\n      })\n      .filter(function(x) {\n        return x;\n      });\n  }\n\n  if (r.TableName === \"MSC_SUPPLIES\") {\n    originalSupply = originalSupply.concat(txIds);\n  }\n\n  if (r.TableName === \"MSC_DEMANDS\") {\n    originalDemand = originalDemand.concat(txIds);\n  }\n}\n\n// unique\noriginalSupply = Array.from(new Set(originalSupply));\noriginalDemand = Array.from(new Set(originalDemand));\n\n\n// ===== STEP 2: Read classified arrays =====\nvar classified = classification.ByTransactionId;\n\nvar releaseSupply = new Set(classified.SupplyOrder.Release || []);\nvar reviewSupply  = new Set(classified.SupplyOrder.Review || []);\n\nvar releaseDemand = new Set(classified.DemandOrder.Release || []);\nvar reviewDemand  = new Set(classified.DemandOrder.Review || []);\nvar supplyExcpArr = classified.SupplyOrder.ReviewException || [];\nvar demandExcpArr = classified.DemandOrder.ReviewException || [];\n\n// ===== STEP 3: Reconciliation – ensure nothing is missed =====\nfor (var i = 0; i < originalSupply.length; i++) {\n  var id = originalSupply[i];\n  if (!releaseSupply.has(id)) {\n    reviewSupply.add(id);\n  }\n}\n\nfor (var i = 0; i < originalDemand.length; i++) {\n  var id = originalDemand[i];\n  if (!releaseDemand.has(id)) {\n    reviewDemand.add(id);\n  }\n}\n\n\n// ===== STEP 4: Build arrays =====\nvar supplyOrdersArr = Array.from(releaseSupply).map(function(x) {\n  return Number(x);\n});\n\nvar demandOrdersArr = Array.from(releaseDemand).map(function(x) {\n  return Number(x);\n});\n\nvar reviewDemandOrdersArr = Array.from(reviewDemand).map(function(x) {\n  return Number(x);\n});\n\nvar reviewSupplyOrdersArr = Array.from(reviewSupply).map(function(x) {\n  return Number(x);\n});\n\n\n// ===== STEP 5: Build payload =====\nvar payload = {\n  planId: planId,\n\n  supplyOrders: supplyOrdersArr,\n  demandOrders: demandOrdersArr,\n  reviewDemandOrders: reviewDemandOrdersArr,\n  reviewSupplyOrders: reviewSupplyOrdersArr,\n\n  OrderRelWorkflowRunId: workflowRunId,\n\n  singleSupplyOrder: null,\n  singleDemandOrder: null,\n  singleReviewSupplyOrder: null,\n  singleReviewDemandOrder: null,\n  supplyReviewException : null,\n  demandReviewException : null\n};\n\npayload.supplyReviewException = supplyExcpArr;\npayload.demandReviewException = demandExcpArr;\n\n\n// ===== STEP 6: Single-order corner case (mutually exclusive) =====\nif (payload.supplyOrders.length === 1) {\n  payload.singleSupplyOrder = payload.supplyOrders[0];\n  payload.supplyOrders = [];\n}\n\nif (payload.demandOrders.length === 1) {\n  payload.singleDemandOrder = payload.demandOrders[0];\n  payload.demandOrders = [];\n}\n\nif (payload.reviewSupplyOrders.length === 1) {\n  payload.singleReviewSupplyOrder = payload.reviewSupplyOrders[0];\n  payload.reviewSupplyOrders = [];\n}\n\nif (payload.reviewDemandOrders.length === 1) {\n  payload.singleReviewDemandOrder = payload.reviewDemandOrders[0];\n  payload.reviewDemandOrders = [];\n}\n\nreturn payload;"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1768854114636"
                  },
                  "code": "GENERATE_PAYLOAD_FOR_NEW_REST",
